## Summary
The `transfer_credits` tool in `src/agent/tools.ts:1014-1043` records the financial transaction in the DB BEFORE the transfer result is checked. On line 1036, `balanceAfterCents` uses a fallback (`transfer.balanceAfterCents ?? Math.max(balance - amount, 0)`) when the API doesn't return the value. If the transfer fails (e.g., network timeout, insufficient funds at the blockchain level), the phantom transaction is still recorded.

## Affected Code
```typescript
// Line 1031-1039: transaction recorded before verifying success
ctx.db.insertTransaction({...});
// The transfer.result was already awaited but errors may be silent
```

## Fix
Record the transaction only after confirming `transfer.status` indicates success, or mark it as 'pending' initially and update on confirmation.

## Summary
The `ChildLifecycle.transition()` method in `src/replication/lifecycle.ts:51-73` throws an error on invalid state transitions but does NOT log the failed attempt or record it in an audit table. An attacker or buggy code could spam invalid transitions without any audit trail. Additionally, `getCurrentState()` throws if the child doesn't exist, but the error message is generic.

## Affected Code
```typescript
// Line 52-57: throws without logging
const current = this.getCurrentState(childId);
const allowed = VALID_TRANSITIONS[current];
if (!allowed || !allowed.includes(toState)) {
  throw new Error(`Invalid lifecycle transition: ${current} → ${toState}`);
}
```

## Fix
Log failed transition attempts to the lifecycle_events table (even for denied transitions), and add a `hasChild()` method to check existence before attempting transitions.
